<title>UK: Ford Halewood decision very surprising - Major.</title>
<headline>Ford Halewood decision very surprising - Major.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister John Major on Thursday described Ford Motor Co's decision to cut 1,300 jobs at its Halewood plant on Merseyside as very surprising and said it ran counter to the trend of growing foreign investment in Britain.  </p>
<p>Major said at question time that Ford's move &quot;flies in the face of most investment decisions which are moving to the UK&quot;.</p>
<p>The British car industry was now more successful than it had been for many years, the prime minister said.</p>
<p>He said Ford's investment plans for its Jaguar luxury cars subsidiary would create 5,000 jobs but this would be of no comfort to Halewood workers.</p>
<p>&quot;I hope it will be possible for them to find alternative employment,&quot; Major said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44 171 542 7767</p>
